{
    "cells": [
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "# Tutorial 3: Fitting Data with PyXspec\n",
                "\n",
                "This tutorial demonstrates how to use `reltrans` within the Python interface of Xspec (PyXspec).\n",
                "This allows you to fit the model to real observational data.\n",
                "\n",
                "**Prerequisites:**\n",
                "- HEASoft (Xspec) installed.\n",
                "- `reltrans` compiled and Xspec-ready (using `make xspec`)."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "import os\n",
                "import sys\n",
                "try:\n",
                "    from xspec import *\n",
                "except ImportError:\n",
                "    print(\"Error: PyXspec is not installed or XSPEC environment variables are not set.\")\n",
                "    print(\"This tutorial requires a full HEASoft installation.\")"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 1. Load the Local Model\n",
                "\n",
                "We use `AllModels.lmod` to load the compiled `reltrans` model into Xspec.\n",
                "Point this to the directory containing the `lmodel.dat` and compiled library (usually `build/xspec`)."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Path to the directory containing lmodel.dat and libxsreltrans.so\n",
                "build_dir = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(os.getcwd(), '../build/xspec'))\n",
                "\n",
                "print(f\"Loading model from: {build_dir}\")\n",
                "try:\n",
                "    AllModels.lmod(\"xsreltrans\", build_dir)\n",
                "    print(\"Model loaded successfully.\")\n",
                "except Exception as e:\n",
                "    print(f\"Failed to load model: {e}\")\n",
                "    print(\"Make sure you ran 'make xspec' successfully.\")"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 2. Load Data\n",
                "\n",
                "Here we would load spectral data files (.pha). Since we don't have real data here, we will simulate strict dummy data or assume a file exists.\n",
                "Replace `data.pha` with your actual data file."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Clear previous data\n",
                "AllData.clear()\n",
                "\n",
                "# Load a dummy spectrum if available, or just demonstrate syntax\n",
                "spectral_file = \"example_data.pha\"\n",
                "\n",
                "if os.path.exists(spectral_file):\n",
                "    s1 = Spectrum(spectral_file)\n",
                "    s1.ignore(\"**-0.5, 10.0-**\") # Example: Ignore bad channels\n",
                "else:\n",
                "    print(f\"Data file '{spectral_file}' not found. Please provide a valid PHA file.\")\n",
                "    # Create a dummy spectrum for demonstration if Xspec allows empty models (it doesn't usually without data for fitting)\n",
                "    # We can fake data:\n",
                "    # fs = FakeitSettings(response=\"resp.rsp\", arf=\"arf.arf\", exposure=1000)\n",
                "    # AllData.fakeit(1, fs)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 3. Define the Model\n",
                "\n",
                "We use the `reltrans` model (usually named `xsreltrans` inside Xspec after loading) combined with absorption (`tbabs`)."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Define model: Absorption * Reltrans\n",
                "m = Model(\"tbabs*xsreltrans\")\n",
                "\n",
                "# Set Parameters\n",
                "# Access parameters by m(index) or m.component.parameter\n",
                "\n",
                "# 1: tbabs nH\n",
                "m.tbabs.nH = 0.1 # 10^21 cm^-2\n",
                "\n",
                "# Reltrans parameters (Verify mapping with 'lmodel.dat' or 'm.show()')\n",
                "m.xsreltrans.a = 0.998\n",
                "m.xsreltrans.inc = 30.0\n",
                "m.xsreltrans.z = 0.01\n",
                "\n",
                "# Fix parameters that we don't want to fit\n",
                "m.xsreltrans.a.frozen = True\n",
                "m.xsreltrans.z.frozen = True\n",
                "\n",
                "print(\"Model Defined:\")\n",
                "m.show()"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 4. Perform Fit\n",
                "\n",
                "We perform a fit using the standard Levenberg-Marquardt algorithm."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "Fit.nIterations = 100\n",
                "Fit.perform()\n",
                "\n",
                "# Show fit results\n",
                "Fit.show()"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 5. Plot Results\n",
                "\n",
                "Visualizing the best-fit model and residuals."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "Plot.xAxis = \"keV\"\n",
                "Plot.device = \"/null\" # Suppress pop-up window\n",
                "Plot(\"data\", \"resid\")\n",
                "\n",
                "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
                "\n",
                "# Extract plot data\n",
                "energies = Plot.x()\n",
                "rates = Plot.y()\n",
                "model = Plot.model()\n",
                "\n",
                "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
                "plt.step(energies, rates, where='mid', label='Data', color='black')\n",
                "plt.step(energies, model, where='mid', label='Model', color='red')\n",
                "plt.xscale('log')\n",
                "plt.yscale('log')\n",
                "plt.xlabel(\"Energy (keV)\")\n",
                "plt.ylabel(\"Counts/s/keV\")\n",
                "plt.legend()\n",
                "plt.show()"
            ]
        }\n
    ],
